    "summary": "Introduce an order payment lifecycle (status, subtotal, paid/failed/cancelled transitions) with a signed payment-provider webhook, admin-initiated refunds with an audit log, a customer order-details endpoint, and an HTML confirmation mail replacing the old notifier.",
    "findings": [
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/admin.ts:19-23",
            "finding": "\"`requireAdmin`\" only rejects non-admins when \"`user.role !== undefined`\", so a user with no role (anonymous) passes, the opposite of what the comment says, and any unauthenticated caller can issue \"`adminRefund`\"."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/webhook.ts:46-48",
            "finding": "The signature is only checked when \"`signature !== undefined`\", so anyone can leave the header off and mark any order \"`paid`\" or \"`failed`\" with a forged payload."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/api.ts:33-37",
            "finding": "\"`handleGetOrder`\" never checks \"`query.customerId`\" against \"`order.customer.id`\", so a signed-in customer can read any other customer's order by guessing the sequential \"`O<n>`\" ids (IDOR)."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/mail.ts:19-20",
            "finding": "The customer-typed discount \"`code`\" goes into the confirmation HTML without \"`escapeHtml`\", unlike the other fields, so arbitrary markup or links can be injected into a shop-branded mail (the code is passed through even when it is not a valid code)."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/refund.ts:26",
            "finding": "\"`refundOrder`\" now refunds \"`order.subtotal`\", the amount before the discount, instead of the \"`total`\" actually paid (and checked in the webhook), so every discounted order is over-refunded."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "COVERAGE",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/admin.ts:30-40",
            "finding": "\"`adminRefund`\" never validates \"`req.amount`\" (it can be negative, non-integer, or larger than \"`order.total`\") and never sums earlier refunds (the new \"`refundsOf`\" is never used), so an order can be refunded any number of times for any amount."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/order.ts:100-108",
            "finding": "\"`markPaid`\"/\"`markFailed`\" apply any state change without checking the current status, so a replayed or late webhook can turn a \"`cancelled`\" order into \"`paid`\" or a \"`paid`\" one into \"`failed`\"; \"`markFailed`\" also never calls \"`releaseAll`\", so stock reserved for declined orders is never released."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/webhook.ts:12",
            "finding": "\"`PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET`\" silently falls back to \"`\"\"`\", so if the environment variable is missing, the HMAC uses a public empty key and anyone can forge signatures; startup should fail instead (and the variable is not documented in \"`README.md`\")."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "INTENT",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "src/api.ts:54-64",
            "finding": "\"`recommendations`\" (a random start-page shuffle) has nothing to do with payments or refunds and is unused, so it is scope creep riding along; the commit message also leaves out the \"`notify.ts`\" to \"`mail.ts`\" replacement and \"`handleGetOrder`\"."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "PROPAGATION",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "src/store.ts:15-17",
            "finding": "The new \"`ordersOf`\" (like \"`refundsOf`\" in \"`src/refund.ts:18`\") has no caller anywhere in the change, so it is dead API that came along without a consumer."
        }
    ]
}
